  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#35808\", \"PowerToys#43402\", \"PowerToys#36355\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before. Keyboard Manager's \\\"Remap a key\\\" list has no Copilot key, because the key sends a shortcut: Win (Left) + Shift (Left) + F23. To remap it, use Keyboard Manager > Remap a shortcut. Click the pencil and press the Copilot key so it records the combination. Then pick the output you want. Remapping it to a single key or an action works for many people. Remapping it to Ctrl (Right) is unreliable. The key can end up acting as Ctrl+Shift, and Ctrl+Alt+Del may not work with it. Some users report that setting the output to Ctrl (Left) works. Another workaround is to edit the recorded shortcut. A dedicated Copilot key option in Keyboard Manager has not been added, and the older tickets don't show a fix. Comments on PowerToys#35808 also say the multi-key output comes from the keyboard's firmware.\"}",
